==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
As the Starred Aliens are pathetically weak here, the only real threat is the singular Zapy. Simply spam anti-Zombie Cats like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], and you should win without much trouble.

If you don't have any strong anti-Zombie Cats, rushing the stage may also work, as the base has a measly 360,000 HP, and Zapy only spawns after 40 seconds.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
-

==='''Chapter 3'''===
While the inclusion of a 1600% Cli-One may complicate things, she is barely even supported as the peons take quite a while to spawn. With her high knockback count, long attack cycle and Maawth being also Floating, [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] is able to capitalize on these opportunities to take out Maawth (Relic Doge can be eliminated with [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]) immediately before moving onto her. Once the Fishmen have her pinned, send [[Talents|Talented]]  [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to quickly tear through her HP before destroying the base.

